  "article_notes": "31 dogs naturally infected with B. canis (Zagreb, Croatia; smear diagnosis, subspecies confirmed by PCR), 18 complicated and 13 uncomplicated, plus 16 healthy controls. All treated with imidocarb; serum cytokines (Luminex) on day 1 (6-8 h after imidocarb) and day 7. One complicated dog died, so day 7 complicated n = 17; no mortality analysis. Complicated = SIRS and/or MODS based on WHO malaria classification (66% of complicated dogs MODS positive, all SIRS positive); the exact criterion for 'complicated' is not fully explicit. Group comparisons are taken from Table 2 (Mann-Whitney p-values); the Results text and Abstract give slightly different p-values for the same comparisons (e.g. MCP-1 day 1 0.00016 in text vs 0.00015 in table; KC-like day 1 0.0324/0.0326/0.03236 vs 0.0322; GM-CSF 0.00068 vs 0.00066; IL-7 0.0002 vs 0.00019; MCP-1 day 7 0.01352 vs 0.013); the table values are used and differences noted per row. Table 2 has a conversion/layout oddity: the 'Diseased day 7' block is labelled 'Healthy(n = 16)' and its Min-Max row is identical to the 'Complicated day 7' Min-Max row; the complicated vs uncomplicated rows themselves read clearly. Statistics are median (and min-max) per group. ROC (Table 4) for day 1 cytokines, HCT day 7 and three linear combinations (LC1-LC3) of cytokines; no p-values or CIs for AUCs (SE given). Not extracted: Table 3 within-group correlations of cytokines with each other and with haematology (not correlations with a severity measure); longitudinal day 1 vs day 7 changes within groups; HCT group comparisons shown only in Fig 5 (vs healthy). skipped_infected_vs_healthy counts markers (9 cytokines + HCT) compared between infected and healthy dogs; 18 cytokine infected-vs-healthy comparisons (2 days) were skipped. Small sample; authors note type 1 error risk and that complicated dogs received different treatment (transfusion if HCT < 20%).",
  "skipped_infected_vs_healthy": 10,
